<h1>Nam Tu Liem by Motorbike: Motorbike Day-Ride Ideas in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Nam Tu Liem is the district whose day rides start before the plan finishes deciding. The boulevards run east through Cau Giay and Ba Dinh to the Old Quarter and Hoan Kiem Lake, they run north toward West Lake and the Tay Ho cafe belt, and westward the suburbs and the open roads begin almost at the doorstep, the city's thinnest edge between a home street and an out-of-town day. The rental counter at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River, hands over the machine, and the menu starts here. This page is a set of day rides built on landmarks and rider comfort, not on invented schedules, because no honest guide quotes a duration for Hanoi traffic.</p>
<p>We cover what a Nam Tu Liem day ride looks like, the West Lake loop day, the long eastern postcard day, the doorstep western day, the river day to Long Bien, folding weather into the menu, choosing the machine for the day, and a flexible week that strings the rides together. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and browse wider riding advice in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>.</p>
